+
+A coalesced delivery was already acknowledged (``202 coalesced``) before any admission, and a
+provider does not resend an acknowledged delivery, so the buffer is the event's only copy. With a
+``spool`` each pending group is also written to a file until its admission commits; a group whose
+admission could not run because the gateway was stopping (ingress withdrawn by the drain before
+the adapter's disconnect flush, or a hard kill) is still there at the next start and is buffered
+again (``restore``). Without one, those events were lost on every restart.
